<!-- @before 1. The Stage Model :: guide -->
### Treat the schedule as a team policy

The chapter’s percentages, tester counts and soak times describe an example rollout policy. Choose them against sample sufficiency, failure reach and operational staffing. Eligibility, installation and observed healthy use remain different measures. [Play staged-rollout behavior](https://support.google.com/googleplay/android-developer/answer/6346149).

<!-- @before 5. Automated Stage Promotion With Crash-Rate Gates :: staff -->
### Unknown evidence must have an explicit outcome

A stale or insufficient sample does not establish safety. Hold exposure while resolving the evidence gap; when a real regression is established, halt and select a lever that reaches the already affected population.
